PROPOSAL ONLY - NOT APPLIED. Producer of quant/data/market/security-master/us-security-master.json
(scripts/market/build-us-security-master.mjs -> quant/engines/us-security-master.js#classifySecurity).

Defect (B2 finding, docs/quant-recovery/v10/population/lifecycle-cases.json, field masterConflict):
  active_status is derived only from the provider endDate (instrument-classification.js: endDate <= staleDays(30) old -> ACTIVE).
  The provider keeps writing the last close forward after a delisting, so endDate stays current and the row stays ACTIVE
  although SEC shows Form 25 / 25-NSE / 15 and (for mergers) an 8-K Item 2.01 completion. Count: see README "Erzeuger-Befund".

Proposed fix: an explicit, source-bound producer input (SEC delisting evidence, built from Form 25/25-NSE/15 + 8-K 2.01/3.01
by the existing SEC fair-access client, never from repeated closes alone) that can only turn a derived ACTIVE into INACTIVE.
It never turns INACTIVE into ACTIVE (same one-way rule as the existing callerSupplied branch). Owner release and a separate
product PR with before/after counts are required (CLAUDE.md: generated artefacts only via their producer; Fachmodelle only in own PR).

